{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDG9CtTNJjDtBCk5iuiV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no vulnerability in `samples/s237.c`, and I've written that verdict to `results/s237.json`.\n\n- **Stack array:** The loop at `samples/s237.c:33-35` writes `ns_addrs[idx]` first, then increments `idx` and stops once it reaches `IEEE80211_BSS_ARP_ADDR_LIST_LEN`. So it only ever writes slots that exist in the array.\n- **Socket buffer (skb) size:** The buffer is allocated with room for the header plus `idx` IPv6 addresses (`sizeof(req_hdr) + idx * sizeof(struct in6_addr)`), and exactly `idx` addresses are added afterwards. Nothing is written past the allocation.\n- **Uninitialized data:** Only the `idx` filled entries of `ns_addrs` are copied out, so no uninitialized stack data is sent.\n- **Locking:** The address list is read while holding `idev->lock`.\n\nThis version looks like the fixed one. A version that wrote the address before checking the limit could overflow the array, but this code checks correctly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":22833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab80af7d-6014-4ee0-b8d6-666a082b147d","uuid":"cb96c827-5b8a-4a8b-bb9e-4cab9ff4b56f","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:50:06.532Z","request_id":"req_011ChDG9CjmvhXtNeK3Fc3Gc"}
